From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 03:24:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8010: Keep the GPU powered over s2idle

The GPU firmware cannot yet be brought back after its power domain was
turned off, so a suspend that gates the GPU leaves rendering dead after
wake. Keep the domain on until the GPU driver can save and restore it.

always-on also keeps the domain powered while awake, including on a
system that renders in software and never binds the GPU driver. Remove
this once the driver handles suspend itself.

Verified on the iPad 6 (J71b) with the GPU desktop across a 69 s sleep.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
index 921c3a570ae4..828342cab683 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8010-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -637,6 +637,8 @@ ps_gfx: power-controller@80328 {
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
 		#reset-cells = <0>;
 		label = "gfx";
+		apple,always-on; /* GPU firmware state cannot be restored yet */
+		apple,manual-pm;
 	};
 
 	ps_sep: power-controller@80400 {
